From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:08:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify WebSocket nonblocking setup failures

Give the existing static constructor diagnostic an event identity while
preserving Info, its full text and constructor continuation. No nonblocking,
SO_NOSIGPIPE, error handling, socket or transport behavior changes.

Add a focused case constructing WebSocketSock with INVALID_SOCKET: the
actual fcntl/ioctlsocket failure records the exact diagnostic as JSON. It
creates no network traffic and never owns or closes a live descriptor.
Platform runtime coverage remains pending; this is not a live-peer test.

Shared eCash WebSocket owner. Source-only event lint/diff checks pass;
new native case NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. Sealed381/current intake unchanged.

Scripted production diff:
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/websocket-nonblocking-diagnostic.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/ws-nonblocking402-conversion.json --apply
